At Stage 0, modifications comprise import housekeeping, the added Apache license,
this attribution notice, baseline documentation and Maven-based CI, replacement
of test CI, and removal of the inherited publishing workflow. Production sources,
grammar, Kotlin tests, fixtures, Maven dependencies, and database settings have
not been changed. See docs/baseline/README.md for provenance and verification.

Stage 1 translates inherited production Kotlin code to Java, adapts annotation
construction in the retained Kotlin tests, confines Kotlin dependencies/tooling
to the test harness, and adds Java caller/MVC verification. The grammar, original
test scenarios/fixtures, and dependency versions are retained. See
docs/stage1/README.md for mechanical language-boundary adaptations and evidence.

Stage 2 translates the inherited test corpus and fixtures to Java, retaining all
113 scenarios and upstream attribution, and removes the Kotlin test toolchain.
Production sources and behavior remain unchanged; see docs/stage2/README.md.

Stage 3 upgrades framework integration to Spring Boot 4.1.1, updates resolver
auto-configuration discovery, and adds PostgreSQL and Java 17/21/25 compatibility
verification. Query implementation, grammar, and original scenarios/fixtures
remain unchanged. New test classes carry 2026 Apache License 2.0 headers. See
docs/stage3/README.md for dependency changes, results, and scope.

Stage 4 adds query-behavior documentation, cross-database characterization tests,
opt-in validation/field restrictions/limits, and structured query diagnostics.
Compatibility defaults and inherited matching strategies remain unchanged. New
classes carry 2026 Apache License 2.0 headers and author/Javadoc documentation.
See docs/stage4/README.md for scope, intentional opt-in rejections, and evidence.

The identity housekeeping milestone renames the project to Pembana Search under
com.pembana:pembana-search:1.0.0-SNAPSHOT and Java packages com.pembana.search.
The annotation package spelling is corrected; the unused deprecated default-package
listener alias is removed. Current documentation and Maven metadata now describe
Pembana Search, and packaged binary/source/Javadoc artifacts retain these notices.
Historical reports and upstream notices keep their original names and identities.
Query behavior, grammar, framework dependencies and tests remain equivalent under
the documented class-name mapping. No publication is configured or performed.

The style/build milestone adds Spring JavaFormat Checkstyle enforcement and
mechanical Java formatting. Builds use JDK 21 while targeting Java 17 and testing
consumer runtimes 17, 21, and 25. Converted Java files credit Spring Search
contributors alongside the fork contributor; existing copyright and MIT notices
remain intact. Query values, assertions, and production instructions are retained.
